{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00207",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 3.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. It's my turn, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.02,
      "end_seconds": 7.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "I've been feeling faint."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.9,
      "end_seconds": 14.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.56,
      "end_seconds": 20.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "About... well, three days. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.3,
      "end_seconds": 29.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Okay, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.41,
      "end_seconds": 50.1,
      "duration_seconds": 19.69,
      "text": "Oh, it sort of comes and goes. I get some relief from sitting in the shade. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. As for pounding headache, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.43,
      "end_seconds": 52.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Has there been muscle cramps too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.62,
      "end_seconds": 55.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "So, yes, about the same, five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.03,
      "end_seconds": 59.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Any confusion or vomiting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.01,
      "end_seconds": 63.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Uh, no. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.43,
      "end_seconds": 65.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Any fainting or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.06,
      "end_seconds": 70.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Um, no, no fainting or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.6,
      "end_seconds": 74.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "So, any fever or passing no urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.19,
      "end_seconds": 76.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.19,
      "end_seconds": 81.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.75,
      "end_seconds": 85.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.38,
      "end_seconds": 87.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.16,
      "end_seconds": 92.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Well, um, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.62,
      "end_seconds": 98.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.32,
      "end_seconds": 109.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "I take losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. It's allopurinol, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.54,
      "end_seconds": 114.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.26,
      "end_seconds": 116.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "It's 100 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.19,
      "end_seconds": 122.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.88,
      "end_seconds": 133.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "Uh, I've got high blood pressure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I have gout, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.81,
      "end_seconds": 134.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.97,
      "end_seconds": 140.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.69,
      "end_seconds": 144.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "One moment, I'm updating your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.46,
      "end_seconds": 161.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Right, carry on. Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.61,
      "end_seconds": 167.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.61,
      "end_seconds": 168.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.59,
      "end_seconds": 173.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.41,
      "end_seconds": 178.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.93,
      "end_seconds": 182.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, no, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.47,
      "end_seconds": 185.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.4,
      "end_seconds": 191.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "So, yes, I had a knee arthroscopy, three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.97,
      "end_seconds": 207.12,
      "duration_seconds": 15.15,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.65,
      "end_seconds": 210.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.8,
      "end_seconds": 214.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.6,
      "end_seconds": 223.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.87,
      "end_seconds": 254.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "Okay: weight 84 kilos, respiratory rate 18, height 182 centimetres, temp 36.4 degrees, BP is 94 over 65, saturation 98 percent, pulse 102."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.49,
      "end_seconds": 257.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.16,
      "end_seconds": 262.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Okay, turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.16,
      "end_seconds": 278.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Capillary refill is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.2,
      "end_seconds": 279.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.81,
      "end_seconds": 283.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.15,
      "end_seconds": 298.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Your skin is warm and a bit clammy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.02,
      "end_seconds": 326.45,
      "duration_seconds": 25.43,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with heat exhaustion with some dehydration at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out an electrolyte imbalance yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.09,
      "end_seconds": 329.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.37,
      "end_seconds": 345.08,
      "duration_seconds": 14.71,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now heat exhaustion with some dehydration is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling faint for three days, and no vomiting or confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.75,
      "end_seconds": 348.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Oh, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.33,
      "end_seconds": 356.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood salts, for dehydration. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 357.54,
      "end_seconds": 360.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "I can book that for Friday at 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.8,
      "end_seconds": 362.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.9,
      "end_seconds": 374.82,
      "duration_seconds": 11.92,
      "text": "I'll start you on ORS, 1 sachet, three times a day, for two days. It's for dehydration. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.34,
      "end_seconds": 378.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.02,
      "end_seconds": 397.1,
      "duration_seconds": 18.08,
      "text": "Avoid the midday sun for a few days and keep a water bottle with you. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Please don't sit on it if you become confused or stop sweating. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.79,
      "end_seconds": 399.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.11,
      "end_seconds": 403.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Let's review you in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.24,
      "end_seconds": 409.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Sure, uh, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.16,
      "end_seconds": 414.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 415.22,
      "end_seconds": 419.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}